identifying solutions</article-title><source>Drugs Aging</source><year>2005</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>559</fpage><lpage>69</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16038571</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fick</surname><given-names>DM</given-names></name><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>JW</given-names></name><name><surname>Wade</surname><given-names>WE</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Updating the Beers criteria for potentially inappropriate medication use in older adults</article-title><source>Arch Intern Med</source><year>2003</year><volume>163</volume><fpage>2716</fpage><lpage>24</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14662625</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Frank</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Conscientious family physicians and polypharmacy</article-title><source>Can Fam Phys</source><year>2002</year><volume>48</volume><fpage>1418</fpage><lpage>20</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="b16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howard</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Dolovich</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Kaczorowski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prescribing of potentially inappropriate medications to elderly people</article-title><source>Fam Pract</source><year>2004</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>244</fpage><lpage>7</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15128683</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b17"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jones</surname><given-names>BA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Decreasing polypharmacy in clients most at risk</article-title><source>AACN Clinical Issues</source><year>1997</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>627</fpage><lpage>34</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9392719</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jorgensen</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Johansson</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Kennerfalk</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Prescription drug use, diagnoses and healthcare utilization among the elderly</article-title><source>Ann Pharmacother</source><year>2001</year><volume>35</volume><fpage>1004</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11573845</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Nusbaum</surname><given-names>NJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Improving elder care by integrating geriatric expertise into medicare</article-title><source>Drugs Aging</source><year>2005</year><volume>22</volume><fpage>371</fpage><lpage>4</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15903350</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b20"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Preskorn</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Multiple medication use in patients seen in the Veterans Affairs healthcare system: So what?</article-title><source>J Psychiatr Pract</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>46</fpage><lpage>9</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15650621</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b21"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Preskorn</surname><given-names>SH</given-names></name><name><surname>Silkey</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Shah</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>Complexity of Medication Use in the Veterans Affairs Healthcare System: Part I: Outpatient Use in Relation to Age and Number of Prescribers</article-title><source>J Psychiatr Pract</source><year>2005</year><volume>11</volume><fpage>5</fpage><lpage>14</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15650617</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="b22"><citation citation-type="web"><collab>US Department of Commerce</collab><article-title>US Census Bureau News: Census Bureau estimates number of adults, older people and school-aged children in states</article-title><year>2004</year><comment>[online]. Accessed March 20, 2007. URL: <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.census.gov/Press-Release/www/releases/archives/population/001703.html"/></comment></citation></ref><ref id="b23"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zarowitz</surname></name><name><surname>Barbara</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Medication overuse and misuse</article-title><source>Geriatr Nurs</source><year>2006</year><volume>27</volume><fpage>204</fpage><lpage>5</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16890100</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>